// General `exists` with NESTING: a user who logged in AND made a transfer
// over 100 — the inner existential (over the transfer amount `a`) is scoped
// by the outer user `u`, and combines a predicate-field restrictor with a
// comparison filter. A broken inner scope (letting another user's large
// transfer satisfy the threshold) would wrongly permit.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Alert",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    exists (u: String). (formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: u } && exists (a: Long). (formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.user: u, input.amount: a } && a > 100))};
